  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Math\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Math\n       Program: commons-math\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/Math.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-math.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 106\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Math-20\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\nabe53a537b4d19a878e8de3735393e0c4e85aa7e\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2012-09-21 14:17:37 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nMATH-864\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MATH-864\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.math3.optimization.direct.CMAESOptimizerTest::testMath864\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Out of bounds (0.5246031767455861 > 0.5)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.math3.optimization.direct.CMAESOptimizer\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: CMAESOptimizer does not enforce bounds\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nThe CMAESOptimizer can exceed the bounds passed to optimize.  Looking at the generationLoop in doOptimize(), it does a bounds check by calling isFeasible() but if checkFeasableCount is zero (the default) then isFeasible() is never even called.  Also, even with non-zero checkFeasableCount it may give up before finding an in-bounds offspring and go forward with an out-of-bounds offspring.  This is against svn revision 1387637.  I can provide an example program where the optimizer ends up with a fit outside the prescribed bounds if that would help.\n\nComments:\n\n[Frank Hess]: Some more info: I see now that FitnessFunction.value will \"repair\" the parameters to be in-bounds before passing them to computeObjectiveValue.  However, the generationLoop does not \"repair\" the parameters when storing the optimum parameter values, it saves the unrepaired values (which may be outside of bounds).\n\n[Gilles Sadowski]: bq. I can provide an example program where the optimizer ends up with a fit outside the prescribed bounds if that would help.\n\nIt would be very helpful if you could set up a unit test (i.e. a minimal example) showing the failure.\nThanks.\n\nbq. the generationLoop does not \"repair\" the parameters when storing the optimum parameter values\n\nThat looks suspicious indeed.\n\n[Frank Hess]: Test program that shows bug.\n\n[Gilles Sadowski]: Thanks for the report, the show-case and the hint toward solving this problem.\nFix committed in revision 1388517. Please test.\n\n[Frank Hess]: Thanks, seems to be fixed testing with revision 1388555.",
  "fix_diff": ""
}